        "problem": "$\\frac{3{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-x-1}{{x}^{2}+x+1}=$",
        "worked_solution": "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3x-5 \\\\  & {x}^{2}+x+1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,3{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-x-1\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+3x}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-5{x}^{2}-4x-1 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,5{x}^{2}-5x-5}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,x+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n- the quotient is $3x-5,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $x+4.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-x-1}{{x}^{2}+x+1}=3x-5+\\frac{x+4}{{x}^{2}+x+1}\n$$",
